From u08a38a1b55af9c04 at groups.google.com  Mon Dec 31 22:20:18 2012
From: u08a38a1b55af9c04 at groups.google.com (Steve Hayes)
Date: Mon, 31 Dec 2012 22:20:18 +0000
Subject: multinomPois when M=1?
Message-ID: <sQQnecUvEi4.KkOf3My3r9gJ@unmarked.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/unmarked/c/sQQnecUvEi4/m/KkOf3My3r9gJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hello All,

Can multinomPois be used to fit a removal model when sampling does not occur in spatially distinct subpopulations?  For example, can the lobster removal analysis in Pollock et al. (1984) (Biometrics 40, 329-340) using effort and temperature covariates be conducted using multnomPois?  I assume this is a situation where M=1; the covariates would be observation level, indexed only on J (# of removals).

Thanks,
Steve Hayes

